  message: "Match-arm dispatch mechanism FIXED in PR #691 (dev d9086c8550). Scoped-done: symptoms #2 (Cmd.run 0 outgoing) and #3 (variant .run() 0 incoming) are resolved with behavioral evidence; symptom #1 (main's chained Cmd::parse().run()) is a DISTINCT mechanism, NOT fixed here, filed as WI-lohup (do not read as resolved).\n\nBehavioral evidence (live analyze_rust probe on the zoxide subcommand shape): 'match self { Cmd::Query(q) => q.run(), Cmd::Add(a) => a.run() }' now yields Cmd::run -> {Query::run, Add::run} (was: both arms collapsed to the last-registered Add::run; Query::run had 0 incoming). Root cause: match-arm tuple-struct-pattern locals were untyped. Fix: _extract_enum_variant_field_types_rust (EnumName::Variant -> positional field types) + bind tuple_struct_pattern locals in the file-scoped var_types map; existing typed-receiver resolution finishes. Covers match/if-let/while-let/destructuring-let; builtin fields + unit/struct-like variants skipped. Tests: test_rust.py::TestRustEnumMatchDispatch (4). rust.py 100% coverage.\n\nEXPLICIT RESIDUAL (WI-lohup): the forward slice from main() still does NOT reach Cmd::run because main's 'Cmd::parse().run()' chained associated-fn call mis-resolves to Add::run (short-name) — needs return-type inference on the chained call, a separate feature from match-arm binding. Overloaded-arity and cross-file enum (registry is file-scoped) are additional documented residuals."  # 02f9
